Sancha of Castile was born on 21 September 1154/5 and died on 9 November 1208, at the age of 54. She was the only surviving child of King Alfonso VII of Castile by his second wife, Richeza of Poland. She married King Alfonso II of Aragon at Zaragoza on January 18, 1174, and had at least eight children who survived into adulthood. Sancha was a patroness of troubadours and became involved in a legal dispute with her husband concerning properties which formed part of her dower estates. She entered the county of Ribagorza in 1177 and took forcible possession of it. Sancha died soon after entering the Monastery of Santa María de Sigena in 1208, where she was interred in front of the high altar of her foundation.
